Assembling Parts with the Assembly Station
Assemble Parts with the AssemblyStation
The AssemblyStation adds mounting parts to a main part, for example doors to a car body, or legs to a
table top as in our example. It moves the mounting parts either to the main MU—according to the value
you enter into the Assembly Table—or it deletes them.
You can insert the AssemblyStation
  into your simulation model from the folder MaterialFlow in the
Class Library or from the toolbar Material Flow in the Toolbox.
In our examples we will:
• Assemble Kitchen Tables
• Always Fill-up the Main MU with Parts
• Assemble Parts Sequentially
• Assemble Kitchen Tables
Compare the sample models: Click the Window ribbon tab, click Start Page > Getting Started > Example
Models > Small Examples. Then, select the respective Category, the Topic, and the Example in the
dialog Examples Collection, and click Open Model.
Assembling Parts with the Assembly Station
10-586 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

