Always Fill-up Main MU with Parts
Always Fill-up the Main MU with Parts
In this basic sample model we demonstrate how to always fill up the main MU, here a pallet, with as many
parts as it can hold. The part type that is loaded onto the pallet does not matter.
We will demonstrate how to:
• Configure the Material Flow to Fill-up Main MU
• Configure the Assembly Table to Fill-up the Main MU
Our finished model looks like this:
Always Fill-up Main MU with Parts
10-602 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Back to Assemble Parts with the AssemblyStation
Configure the Material Flow to Fill-up Main MU
Insert the material flow objects, so that they match the screenshot below. Make sure that all objects are
connected. Then configure the material flow objects.
• Our first step in configuring the material flow to fill-up the main mu is to duplicate the Part twice. We
named the duplicated parts PartRed and PartBlue and assigned them the respective colors. We also
duplicated the Container.
Configure the Material Flow to Fill-up Main MU
Plant Simulation Help 10-603
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• The Source named SourceMainParts produces two types of Containers, as specified in the ProductsTable,
in a sequential sequence.
• The SourceMainParts sends the pallets along a Conveyor to the AssemblyStation.
• The Source named SourceParts produces two types of Parts with different colors, as specified in the
PartsTable, in a cyclical sequence.
Configure the Material Flow to Fill-up Main MU
10-604 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• The SourceParts sends the PartBlue on to the ParallelStation named BlueParts. We entered the settings
below. We cleared Start Processing When Full to fill up the pallet with different part types. We also
entered a processing time of 10 seconds on the Tab Times.
• The SourceParts sends the PartRed on to the ParallelStation named RedParts. We entered the settings
below. We cleared Start Processing When Full to fill up the pallet with different part types. We also
entered a processing time of 10 seconds on the Tab Times.
Configure the Material Flow to Fill-up Main MU
Plant Simulation Help 10-605
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• The ParallelStations send the processed parts on to the AssemblyStation which loads them onto the
pallets.
Back to Always Fill-up the Main MU with Parts
Configure the Assembly Table to Fill-up the Main MU
To make our AssemblyStation load the processed blue and red parts onto the pallets and always fill up the
pallets to their capacity, namely four parts, we selected Assembly Table > Fill-up Main MU. We did not
change any other settings.
Although Fill-up Main MU is listed as an option of the Assembly Table, the AssemblyStation does not use
an Assembly Table at all, but accepts parts from any of its predecessors until the capacity of the main MU,
our Container, is reached.
Configure the Assembly Table to Fill-up the Main MU
10-606 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

When we run the simulation, we see that the AssemblyStation always fills up the pallets, i.e., it places four
parts on each and every pallet. Some pallets are filled up with red parts only, some with blue parts only,
and some with a mix of both part types just as their processing on the ParallelStations is finished.
The AssemblyStation then sends the loaded pallets on a Conveyor on to the Drain.
Using an Assembly Table with the Setting MU Types
Let's compare the setting Fill-up Main MU with the setting Assembly Table > MU Types in the Example
model > AssemblyStation > Change Assembly List.
In this model the parts are moved on according to the settings specified in the Assembly Table and to the
Entrance Control named setBOM.
Configure the Assembly Table to Fill-up the Main MU
Plant Simulation Help 10-607
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

When we run the simulation, we see, that the AssemblyStation loads the processed parts in a mixed
sequence depending on the time their processing is finished onto the pallets. It never fills them up to their
capacity, before sending them on to the Drain though.
Back to Always Fill-up the Main MU with Parts
