Configure the Assembly Table to Assemble Parts Sequentially
We configured the sequential assembly of the arriving parts in the Assembly Table of the AssemblyStation
by typing in the Assembly Time and the Sequence Number.
We proceeded as follows:
• We selected Depends on Main MU and clicked Open to open the Assembly Table.
• We use these settings to assemble the parts:
◦ We place an Amount of 1 PartA into BoxA. This assembly process takes an Assembly Time of 5
minutes . The Sequence Number 1 determines that PartA is put into the box before PartB.
◦ We place an Amount of 2 PartB into BoxA. This assembly process takes an Assembly Time of 10
minutes . The Sequence Number 2 determines that PartB is put into the box after PartA.
◦ We place an Amount of 1 PartB into BoxB. This assembly process takes an Assembly Time of 3
minutes . The Sequence Number 1 determines that PartB is put into the box before PartA.
Configure the Assembly Table to Assemble Parts Sequentially
10-614 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

◦ We place an Amount of 2 PartA into BoxB. This assembly process takes an Assembly Time of 6
minutes . The Sequence Number 2 determines that PartA is put into the box after ParB.
Run the simulation and watch how the AssemblyStation places the specified parts into the specified boxes
in the sequence which we defined.
To follow the assembly process step-by-step, open the Event Debugger.
Back to Configure the Material Flow to Assemble Parts Sequentially
Back to Assemble Parts Sequentially
